<%#
  The run as one growing list: every step answered so far, then whatever the run
  is waiting on — the open card, a Resume control, or its ending.

  This is what replaces the wizard's one-card-at-a-time page. The problem it
  solves is orientation — an agent on a call losing their place because the page
  jumps and resets every step — not re-reading, which is why rows carry a
  summary rather than the script.

  The tail lives inside the list on purpose. Whatever the run is waiting on
  carries id="runner-card-current", so a streamed answer always has something to
  replace: if the Resume control or the ending sat outside the list, a POST from
  those states would stream into a target that does not exist.

  Both runners render this; the difference between them lives in the shells,
  which pass everything route-shaped as a local.

  locals: scenario, step, next_url, stop_url, back_button, show_cancel,
          errors, submitted, auto_advance, parked, results_url
%>
<ol class="runner-thread" id="runner-thread" data-controller="thread">
  <% runner_thread_entries(scenario).each do |entry| %>
    <% if entry["kind"] == "group_start" %>
      <%= render "runner/thread_group", entry: entry %>
    <% else %>
      <%= render "runner/thread_row", entry: entry %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "runner/thread_tail",
        scenario: scenario, step: step, parked: parked, results_url: results_url,
        next_url: next_url, stop_url: stop_url, back_button: back_button,
        show_cancel: show_cancel, errors: errors, submitted: submitted,
        auto_advance: auto_advance %>
</ol>
